{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788971447,"nonce":"PX+rJVSR9J6RIcrYedJTOrHfyf8=","title":"losses gauge counts every COMPLETED construction as a loss, and advance halts on it","message":"The `losses` gauge and the new `loss` stop kind fire on a frame that completed successfully. Found on the first day of openrun-20260909, the first game run on the 2026-09-09 changes.\n\n## What happened\n\nThree `Bed` blueprints placed at t~1000. At t7208 an advance halted:\n\n    STOP: loss | bed (building)\n\n`gauges.losses`:\n\n    {\"thing\": 37364, \"def\": \"Bed\", \"label\": \"bed\", \"kind\": \"frame\",\n     \"at\": [110, 130], \"tick\": 7208, \"ticks_ago\": 14, \"mode\": \"Vanish\"}\n\n`things {def:\"Bed\", detail:true}` at the same moment:\n\n    Bed count on map: 1\n      id 37381 at [110, 130] hp 100\n\n**The bed was finished, not destroyed.** id 37364 is the frame; id 37381 is the bed that replaced it, at the same cell, at full health.\n\n## The mechanism\n\n`RimWorld/Frame.CompleteConstruction(Pawn worker)` (decompiled 1.6, line 280) calls the parameterless `Destroy()` on the frame — which is `DestroyMode.Vanish` — and then `GenSpawn.Spawn`s the finished thing at line 320.\n\nThe gauge's own `basis` string says it subtracts \"the five DestroyMode values that are the colony's own work (Deconstruct, WillReplace, Cancel, Refund, FailConstruction)\". **`Vanish` is not in that list, and `Vanish` is how every successful build ends.** The five excluded modes cover cancelling and failing; the one mode that means *success* is the one that gets through.\n\n## Why this is p1\n\n- Every building the colony ever completes halts the clock with `stop.kind: \"loss\"`. On a build-heavy day that is a halt per element.\n- Losses are a LEVEL and `write-off` is not built (975973e's second half), so the false levels accumulate and **nothing can clear them** — the gauge says so itself in `clears_with`.\n- It poisons the one signal the gauge exists for. The spec's own motivating case is a manhunter pack destroying two turrets and an autocannon while the journal recorded nothing; a gauge that also counts every completed wall cannot be read for that.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A frame that completes registers no loss and does not halt an advance. Reproduce: place any blueprint, advance until built, read `gauges.losses` — `total` unchanged, no `loss` stop.\n- The discriminator is not the mode alone. `Vanish` is genuinely ambiguous: `Frame.CompleteConstruction` uses it for success, and other paths use it for real removal. Distinguish by what the frame became — the completed thing is spawned at the same position in the same call — or hook `CompleteConstruction` rather than the destroy.\n- A REAL destruction still registers: `dev:destroy` a built wall and a frame under construction; both appear with the right `kind` and `mode`, and the advance halts.\n- The `basis` string is updated to say what is actually excluded, since it is currently a false statement about behaviour.\n- A `destroyed` journal row obeys the same rule — check whether the row and the gauge share a filter or duplicate it.","files":null}]}